    "created_at": "2016-01-31T00:44:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-31T00:44:56Z",
    "body": "Basically we need to be able to draw text with the equivalent of control over the following CSS properties:\n- font-variant-ligatures\n- font-variant\n- font-feature-settings\n\nBut CRC2D only exposes a single \"font\" attribute that is a subset of the CSS font shorthand.\n\nA yucky solution would be to add more attributes. A better solution might be to have a separate Font object that could be constructed and assigned to \"font\" (which I think @zcorpan was raising as an issue anyway).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
